###############################################################################
### USAGE GUIDE
###############################################################################
###
### How to Use This HTTP Client File:
###
### STEP 1: Get CSRF Token (Required for all POST/PATCH/DELETE requests)
###    - Run the "Get CSRF Token" request in the "CSRF Token Setup" section
###    - The response handler script will automatically extract the XSRF-TOKEN
###      cookie and set the {{csrfToken}} variable
###    - You can verify this in the HTTP Client environment variables
###
### STEP 2: Register or Login
###    - To register: Use "Register New User" (already has CSRF token configured)
###    - To login: Use "Login User" (already has CSRF token configured)
###    - After successful login, extract the laravel_session cookie value
###    - Manually set: @sessionCookie = <your-session-cookie-value>
###
### STEP 3: Make Authenticated Requests
###    - All authenticated requests already include proper Cookie headers
###    - They will use {{sessionCookie}} and {{csrfToken}} variables
###
### Important Notes:
###
### • CSRF Protection:
###   - All POST/PATCH/DELETE requests require both:
###     * X-CSRF-TOKEN header with the token value
###     * XSRF-TOKEN cookie with the same token value
###   - The "Get CSRF Token" request handles this automatically
###
### • Authentication:
###   - Authenticated routes require the laravel_session cookie
###   - You must manually extract and set {{sessionCookie}} after login
###
### • Request Headers:
###   - X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest (for AJAX requests)
###   - Accept: application/json (for JSON responses)
###   - Content-Type: application/json (for JSON payloads)
###
### • Inertia.js Requests (optional):
###   - Add X-Inertia: true header
###   - Add X-Inertia-Version: {version} header
###
### • Permissions:
###   - Mentor routes require 'mentor' role assigned to the user
###   - Some routes may require specific permissions
###
### • File Uploads:
###   - Not included in this file
###   - Use Content-Type: multipart/form-data
###   - Adjust request format accordingly
###
###############################################################################
